 he and my oldest brother Eric  had waited outside the old garden in New  York to get Bill Russell autograph and  how Bill when Bill Russell had come out  he had barked at them because of course  you notoriously doesn't sign autographs  I was thinking dad didn't you know that  back then like I hope it wasn't sold out  that you were standing out there waiting  but um I think only because bill had he  was so you know he's so legendary he's  so accomplished I mean and he's lived so  much history I mean back to some of the  you know some of the early milestones we  were talking about before I mean he was  there you know when Martin Luther King  you know made his famous civil rights  speech you know in Washington DC and and  so he intimidates me a little bit as a  historical figure  just because he's seen so much and as I  always say to people you know about the  NBA they forget what a young league we  are I mean it's it's like if you worked  in baseball and somebody said you want  to sit with Babe Ruth you know at a game  that's what to me it's like sitting with  Bill Russell yeah now your job is  obviously all-consuming I don't know if  there's time for anything else but what  are you doing when you're not watching  basketball or otherwise managing the  league any outside hobbies well I enjoy  running still I think you know I've run  two marathons over the years I'm not  running such long distances anymore but  I try to find time to run I'm fortunate  to live near Central Park and I have a  dog I have a Labrador Retriever and in  New York one of the greatest things  about New York City is that before 9:00  a.m. and after 9:00 p.m. you don't have  to have your dog on its leash on its  leash in Central Park so that's sort of  really fun kind of hobby you know  relaxation for me go  at the park with my dog and throwing the  ball and stuff like that I don't watch  as much non sports television as I used  to I find that it's pretty all-consuming  when with the amount of mba programming  on the amount of NBA coverage there is  on the internet but I love movies you  know I I try to get to as many movies as  I can last one you saw oh my god it's  such an unfair question I got to think  for a second we can we can move on Steve  Ballmer new one over the LA Clippers you  mentioned him earlier  a very energetic guy described him in 20  words or less he is the most  enthusiastic person I've ever met  i sat with him at a Clippers game before  he bought the team and he was bellowing  so loud I mean I I generally don't sit  with owners at games but he wasn't an  owner there but people kept looking  around like what's that noise emanating  from my row and it was Steve yelling and  screaming and just with the crazy  enjoyment and enthusiasm during the game  but I should say on a serious note he's  extraordinarily smart again he just  attended his first Board of Governors  meetings cast a lot of really good  probing questions about materials and as  I said to him afterwards talk about a  fresh look I think when you have a new  set of eyes on materials that we've been  historically giving to teams whether  it's the way we present our financials  whether it's the way we talk about  basketball and it's some money as  accomplished as Steve Ballmer or  somebody who you know was the CEO of one  of the most successful companies in the  world it's like please you know come in  the tent and like make suggestions to us  yeah we talked a little bit about  innovation so three things that are  still on the Adam silver board and not  things that have to happen just things  you'd like to do in Bay 2 at least  consider the format of the season is  something I'm very focused on and  whether that means expanding it in a way  that allows more rests for the players  over the course of the season means  starting a little bit earlier maybe  going a little bit later that's one of  the things on my list  as we just did to new media deals in the  United States obviously we renewed with  our great partners at Turner and ESPN  and ABC but I think their enormous  opportunities international  internationally and and not just revenue  generating but for a much more  comprehensive coverage and that's as  much about what these new deals were  about I was just recently in China  there's some media companies there that  literally blow away anything that's  happened in the United States in terms  of the numbers of users of those of  those apps on social media the kinds of  technology they're using so that's and  that's incredibly fascinating to me and  I say lastly just just to name three I  continue to be consumed with the way we  can be represented visually around the  world it's something I talk about a lot  and that is well the in arena experience  is critically important especially if  you're watching a game on TV if there's  not an excited crowd around the game you  know it's you're not necessarily to be  as in food as enthusiastic a viewer if  you don't see people excited to be there  but having said that such a miniscule  fraction of our fans ever get to  experience our game in the arena not  just the United States but I can work in  the United States but more so  internationally and I think the ultimate  goal is how do we replicate that  experience how do we make it feel when  you're watching a game on television  when you have whatever mobile devices  tablets and phones with you that you  have that sense that you're part of that  larger community that people are yelling  and screaming that you can react that  you can pick angles you can look at  replays that that to me you know making  enhancing that experience for people who  are watching through whatever form of  media is on the top of my is at the top  of my agenda as well before we let you  go  we want to look a little bit even  further ahead into the future here 2024  10 years down the road a few predictions  and don't worry we're not going to hold  you to of these but true or false 2024  in the Year 2024 there will be a female  head coach in the NBA true 2020 for the  NBA we'll have teams in Europe  I know it's on the 10 year rolling cycle  that David put out there 20 years ago  but I you know I don't want to pretend I  can predict the future I don't know no  okay  true or false there will be more teams  in the United States in 2024 I think  it's possible teams could be in some  different markets but expansion is not  on our agenda right now so I won't send  the congratulations card to Seattle just  yet you know it's a difficult issue  because I I don't want to prejudge it I  think 30 teams feels right at the moment  again though I don't want to predict the  influx of great players I mean part of  it it's not just a financial issue but  it's a competitive issue and where as  you and I talked about the at the  beginning of this session we're seeing  more competitive teams than we've had  any time in history just a few years ago  reporters like you were writing that  this diluted league wasn't producing  great competition every night so the  last thing I want to do is quickly talk  about adding more teams I know I'm not  working in your foot that's ok we're not  you and I fight not the lightening part  I got to speed you up all right in the  year 2024 the NBA will have a true minor  league system 30 d-league teams with 30  affiliations with the top NBA teams true  true that would be that would be a great  move in the year 2020 for LeBron James  will have equaled Michael Jordan with  six championships I'm not making any  pretty championship calls that's that's  fair enough  easier one for you here I think the year  2020 for Gregg Popovich will have  retired as coach of the San Antonio  Spurs and will be a sideline reporter  for one of the true the greatest thing  wouldn't it I would love to see him turn  the tables and finally in the year 2024  Adam silver will be Commissioner of the  NBA  boy that's the last prediction I'm gonna  make I mean especially I'm not gonna  speak for our owners all I can say is  I'm fully engaged right now and I love  my job  fantastic thank you very much Adam  silver Adam Silver Commissioner of the  NBA here with us at bleacher report  Thank You Howard Adam thank you
 

